Top-level layout is flat and organised by artefact type, not by V-model phase: arch/ rtl/ model/ constraints/ prj/ scripts/ docs/. Rationale: artefacts cross phases (MDS is authored in arch phase, referenced during implementation, cited during verif); tools and humans search by artefact type. V-model review gates (G1–G5) live in arch/README.md, not in folder names.


| V-model phase | Artefacts | Where they live |
|---|---|---|
| Requirements | RTM, SYS-*/SFU-* citations | `arch/rtm.md`, FAD §1.5 |
| Architecture | FAD, ICDs, ADRs | `arch/fad/`, `arch/icd/`, `arch/adr/` |
| Module design | MDSs | `arch/modules/` |
| Implementation | RTL, constraints, refmodels | `rtl/`, `constraints/`, `model/` |
| Unit verification | Unit TBs, coverage | verif repo `cocotb/` |
| Integration verification | UVM, system tests | verif repo `uvm/` |
| Integration | Vivado project, bitstream | `prj/` |
